# Live-model configuration for the JEXI acceptance run — TEMPLATE.
#
# Copy to `live-model.config.env`, fill in your own key, and keep the copy
# untracked. The real file is matched by `.gitignore` (`*.config.env`) and the
# template is explicitly un-ignored, so this file is safe to commit.
#
#   cp live-model.config.env.example live-model.config.env
#   chmod 600 live-model.config.env
#   set -a; . ./live-model.config.env; set +a
#   node --test tests/live/live-model-dahl.test.js
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SUBSTITUTION NOTE — read this before comparing against the original request.
#
# The originally requested model was deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731, to be
# served by the dahl gateway at https://inference.dahl.global/v1. That endpoint
# is live and reachable, but BOTH credentials tried against it were rejected:
#
#     POST /v1/chat/completions -> 401
#     {"error":{"code":"invalid_api_key","message":"invalid API token"}}
#
# Groq does not serve DeepSeek at all. Of the 11 models a working Groq key can
# reach, the tool-capable ones verified to emit a real fs_read(...) tool call
# rather than prose are:
#
#     openai/gpt-oss-120b     (default here; strongest verified tool-caller)
#     qwen/qwen3.8-27b
#     openai/gpt-oss-20b
#
# Everything downstream of the model is unchanged and real: the sandbox, the
# pytest execution, the exit codes, and the independent TestVerifier.
#
# Health-check warning: GET /v1/models on the dahl gateway returns 200 with
# NO credential at all. Only a POST to /v1/chat/completions actually validates
# a key. Do not verify credentials against a /models endpoint.

# Your key goes here.
ARCEN_MODEL_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=

ARCEN_MODEL_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
ARCEN_MODEL_NAME=openai/gpt-oss-120b
ARCEN_MODEL_PROVIDER=groq
